{"type":"text","timestamp":1787239909282,"sessionID":"ses_fe0351b4fffe7VpaVYC1FvmN79","part":{"id":"prt_01fcc99a8001zXZ37QRRKAwqwz","messageID":"msg_01fcc932f001WIrSWpEnz8yfZ9","sessionID":"ses_fe0351b4fffe7VpaVYC1FvmN79","type":"text","text":"Baseline confirmed failing (2/2 pagination tests failed before my change). My change makes all pagination tests pass. Final state of `src/pagination.ts:1`:\n\n```ts\nexport function pageSlice<T>(items: readonly T[], page: number, pageSize: number): T[] {\n  if (!Number.isInteger(page) || page < 1) {\n    throw new RangeError(\"page must be a 1-based integer\");\n  }\n  if (!Number.isInteger(pageSize) || pageSize < 1) {\n    throw new RangeError(\"pageSize must be a positive integer\");\n  }\n  const start = (page - 1) * pageSize;\n  return items.slice(start, start + pageSize);\n}\n```\n\nChanged pagination to 1-based (`start = (page - 1) * pageSize`), added integer/positive validation throwing `RangeError`, and left all other modules untouched. Pagination tests pass; the unrelated failing suites (config, discount, email, money, sku) fail identically on the unmodified baseline.","time":{"start":1787239897512,"end":1787239909279}}}
